1 NOTE Izabel da Silva, of Torres Novas (comarca de Tomar, arcebispado/patriarcado de Lisboa), came to Brazil with her husband João Carneiro da Fontoura about 1730. They stopped first in Minas Gerais, where
2 CONC  their first daughter Francisca Veloso was born at Congonhas do Campo about 1729. They then lived in Rio de Janeiro and reached the new Presídio do Rio Grande in 1737, later moving to Viamão and Rio Pa
