1 NOTE Possible identification: Claude Nicolas Doux is probably the French actor, director and teacher Émile/Emílio Doux (b. France 1798, Conservatoire de Paris, d. Rio de Janeiro 1876). He was in Lisbon fro
2 CONC m Dec 1834 to 1851, living at rua do Salitre 22 in 1848, and in Rio de Janeiro from 1851. In Rio he was director of the Teatro S. Pedro and the Ginásio, taught French and declamation, and published a
2 CONC  French grammar in 1874. He received a Brazilian carta de naturalização in 1864 (Almanak Laemmert 1865). Evidence for the identification: (1) the parents Nicolas Doux and Catherine-Agnès Magny were in
2 CONC  Paris, and she (b. c.1776) could be the mother of a son born in 1798. (2) The son 'Emílio Nicolau' was born in Lisbon in 1841, while Émile Doux was working there. (3) Ernesto (1852) and Maria (1858) w
2 CONC ere born in Rio, after Émile moved there in 1851. (4) Alfredo was called a 'capitalista francez' in 1904. (5) Alfredo's grandson was named Henry Robert Emile Doux. (6) A 'Nicolau Doux' is recorded in
2 CONC  Rio in 1861. Against: the tree's birth estimate of c.1813, and no record yet links the name Claude Nicolas to Émile. To confirm, find the 1841 Lisbon baptism of Emílio Nicolau, the 1864 naturalization
2 CONC  file or the 1876 death entry. (research 2026-11-21, possible)
