1 NOTE Leandro Artayeta, native of Buenos Aires, son of Bernardo Artayeta and Estefanía Centurión, married Maria Herculana da Fontoura Palmeiro (b. Rio Grande 1803, d. Porto Alegre 1831). He died in Porto Al
2 CONC egre in 1830 (Genealogia Riograndense, via Koren de Lima). Their children, all born in Porto Alegre: Maria Leandrina (1826-1902), Amália Herculana (1827-1897, m. 1849 her uncle Capt. Francisco Eleutér
2 CONC io da Fontoura Palmeiro), Emília Josefina (1828-1880, m. 1850 her uncle José Maria da Fontoura Palmeiro), José Leandro (1829) and Ana Cândida (1830). Inventory of 'Leandro Artayeta e sua mulher Maria
2 CONC  Herculana da Fontoura Palmeira': Porto Alegre, I Vara de Família e Sucessão, 1831, processo 1061A (APERS). Earlier he was a 'teniente segundo' of grenadiers in Belgrano's army (Documentos del Archivo
2 CONC  de Belgrano), and a Uruguayan study (Cabrelli, 'Presencia masónica en la Cisplatina') calls him consul at San Borja and son-in-law of the Rio Grande mason Palmeiro. (research 2026-11-21, probable)
