3 TEXT Sébastien-Nicolas Gachet a vu le jour à Paris le 27 octobre 1770. Cet enfant légitime de Joseph-Emmanuel-Eloy Gachet et de Marguerite-Marie née Zürich a reçu le baptême en l'église Saint-Sulpice. Sa m
4 CONC ère, originaire probablement de Lessoc dans le canton de Fribourg, avait déjà été baptisée dans la même paroisse. Aucune indication ne mentionne l'activité du père de Sébastien dans la capitale frança
4 CONC ise.
1 NOTE What the Swiss literature says about his family (Nicoulin, La genèse de Nova Friburgo, 1973, pp. 33-35 and notes pp. 325-326, from the burgess book of the commune of Gruyères, pp. 58-59, and Fribourg
2 CONC  notarial acts). Born in Paris on 27 Oct 1770 and baptised at Saint-Sulpice, legitimate son of Joseph-Emmanuel-Eloy Gachet and Marguerite-Marie Zürich. Nicoulin shows that the old story (Marro, Reichle
2 CONC n) is legend: he was not born at Gruyères as one of twelve children of a poor joiner named Laurent, the school friendship with Murat at a Versailles seminary is 'fantaisie', and he was not a slave in
2 CONC  Algiers in 1815. In Paris he was a merchant (lease of a flat, 6 ventôse an IX; a 'transport' of 28 frimaire an XII showing business with Claude Coquet, silk merchant of Lyon; on 9 Feb 1803 licensed to
2 CONC  supply ship timber to the port of Toulon; later a creditor of the Empire for 38,106.15 francs). On 4 Nov 1812 his mother, by notarial act in the canton of Fribourg (AEF, RN 4770), consented to his ma
2 CONC rriage and called him 'inspecteur au trésor du royaume de Naples'; he married Marie-Thérèse Chambelland at Naples, 'probablement une française'. The Gruyères burgess book enters his son Adolphe-Joseph
2 CONC -Alcidio, born 27 Jun 1812 and baptised in the parish of Sainte-Marie des Anges (Santa Maria degli Angeli) at Naples, and his daughter Marie-Marguerite-Joséphine, born at Gruyères on 18 Mar 1815, her
2 CONC  father being present. From 1815 he bought land and borrowed money in the Gruyère (acts of 17 Aug 1815, 28 Sep 1816, 4 Nov 1816); on 20 Nov 1815 he bought at auction the baths of Montbarry (Le Pâquier)
2 CONC  from 'M. Joseph Gachet, président du Conseil communal de Gruyères'; on 5 May 1817 he took a passport for Brazil at the prefecture of Gruyères. A description quoted by Nicoulin makes him short with a
2 CONC  malformed back (Reichlen: a hump 'comparable à celle d'Esope'). Letters of his wife survive in the Arquivo Nacional, Rio de Janeiro (Colonia de Nova Friburgo, caixa 991, pac. 1). Neither Nicoulin nor
2 CONC  the HLS gives his death; Reichlen (1897) only says that he died in Brazil 'laissant une veuve et deux enfants dans une situation de fortune presque précaire'. No brothers or sisters of his were found
2 CONC  in the Swiss literature. (research 2026-11-23, probable)
