2 CONC acques 1652-1700, François-Pierre-Emmanuel 1688-1724 (curial; note the given name Emmanuel), Tobie 1707-1753, Jean-Joseph 1740-1754, Henri 1758-1768, Nicolas 1786-1832. Which of the 18th-century Gache
2 CONC ts was 'the lieutenant', father of Joseph-Emmanuel-Eloy, is not established. (3) Another Gruyères Gachet in Paris: François Gachet, 'premier conseiller du Roi à l'Ile de Bourbon', died in Paris in 177
